-# Every blob a merge adds stays in every clone and every CI checkout forever, even after a later
-# commit deletes it. In three summer months main received a 2 MB PR screenshot, a 2 MB
-# default.tar.gz, PR infographics, a Windows cache database and a 1 MB fuzz corpus, none of
-# which any check looked at. Edits to existing text files are left to the code-health
-# FILE_LINES ratchet. Exact-path exceptions live in .github/blob-size-allowlist.txt
-# (CODEOWNERS-reviewed). Local: `python scripts/check --only blob-size`.
-#
-# Runs unconditionally (no change-classifier gate): a docs-only or asset-only PR skips the
-# Python and frontend lanes, and that is exactly the kind of PR that commits a screenshot.
